  "verbalization": "Garcinone E is shown to have a target relationship with Raji, which is then implicated in targeting the CD276 antigen through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Garcinone E may act as a modulator of Raji cells, which in turn interact with CD276 antigen through various compounds, including 3-(1H-Benzimidazol-2-Yl)-7-(Diethylamino)Chromen-2-One, 6-Hydroxycoumarin, and Dianversicoside G. These compounds appear to share a common mechanism of targeting CD276 antigen, indicating a potential convergent pathway. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target relationships suggests that CD276 antigen may be a key downstream target in the signaling network activated by Garcinone E. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Garcinone E influences Raji cells in a manner that indirectly engages CD276 antigen, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling cascades. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that Garcinone E may exert its biological effects by modulating Raji cells, which then interact with CD276 antigen via multiple mediators.",
